      <p>The backend is Go with Gin, using go-git for storage and goldmark for markdown and frontmatter parsing. Note content lives in git repositories on disk; tags, audit records and webhook state go in SQLite by default (zero config) or PostgreSQL. Events flow through an embedded NATS JetStream, so there is no external broker to run. Tracing, metrics and structured logs come from OpenTelemetry, Prometheus and zap.</p>

      <h2>Interesting bits</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Edits land as git commits</strong>, GPG-signed for integrity. Version history, per-note history browsing and restore-to-any-version come for free.</li>
        <li><strong>Graph queries</strong> cover backlinks, outlinks, N-hop neighbours, shortest path between two notes, orphan detection, cycle detection and clustering.</li>
        <li><strong>A write buffer</strong> batches commits, so a burst of edits does not turn into a burst of tiny commits.</li>
        <li><strong>Webhooks</strong> are HMAC-SHA256 signed, with circuit breakers, rate limiting, delivery history and a dead-letter queue for the ones that keep failing.</li>
        <li><strong>Live updates</strong> arrive over WebSocket, with subscriptions per note, per repository, for the graph or for system events.</li>
        <li><strong>The frontend</strong> is a CodeMirror editor with vim mode, alongside a D3 force-directed graph view, daily notes, a timeline, a tag browser, and offline support as a PWA.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it ships</h2>
      <p>CI runs the Go tests under the race detector, scans with govulncheck, gosec and Trivy, validates the API against its OpenAPI contract, and runs Playwright end-to-end tests, k6 load tests and smoke tests against a throwaway kind cluster. Releases build multi-arch container images that are cosign-signed with SBOMs attached, and Flux GitOps deploys them onto the homelab cluster on the <a href='/server.html'>server rack</a>.</p>

